Quite true; but the musical instrument I want to start the bard with is
NOT magical. It is a plain, ordinary instrument.    The magic is in the
bard, not the tool.  That's why Bards can do things with songs other
classes cannot.

In fact, if the bard *loses* his/her instrument, finding something as
simply as a tooled horn should bring a fiendish grin to the player's
lips -- because now he/she is *armed* again. Something no other class
particularly cares about.

Of course, what happens when a magical bard gets ahold of a magical
instrument ... well, that could be interesting.  Might have some
implications for the quest artifact, but I haven't thought that through
yet. 

